{"id":"NCT04682483","title":"Cardiogenic Shock Working Group Registry","official":"Cardiogenic Shock Working Group Registry","summary":"The Cardiogenic Shock Working Group is a multicenter registry where we collect de-identified clinical variables from the medical records and follow-up phone calls of shock patients from multiple institutions and centralize this data to a single registry for analysis of clinical outcomes.","conditions":["Cardiogenic Shock"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"Vasopressor"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Inotrope"},{"type":"DEVICE","name":"Acute Mechanical Circulatory Support Devices"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Patients must have cardiogenic shock.\n\nCardiogenic shock is defined by at least one of the two categories below:\n\n1. At least 2 of the following concurrently at any point during the index hospitalization:\n\n   * Cardiac Index \\< 2.2\n   * PAPI \\< 1.0\n   * Cardiac Power Output ≤ 0.6\n   * MAP \\< 60mmHg or a \\>30mmHg drop in MAP from baseline\n   * SBP \\< 90mmHg or a \\>30mmHg drop in SBP from baseline\n   * Pulse \\> 100\n2. Require at least one acute mechanical circulatory support device, vasopressor or inotrope to maintain values above the above target.\n\nPost-cardiotomy patients must meet the inclusion criteria 72 hours after their surgery to be included in this registry.","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":20000,"start":"2017-12-04","pcd":"2027-12","upd":"2026-10-27","sponsor":"Tufts Medical Center","areas":["other","rare"],"central":["Navin K Kapur, MD · 6176368252 · nkapur@tuftsmedicalcenter.org"],"sites":[{"f":"Cleveland Clinic Florida","city":"Weston","pr":"Florida","zip":"33331","s":"R","lat":26.1004,"lon":-80.3998,"c":"Jaime Hernandez-Montfort, MD MPH"},{"f":"Northwestern Medicine","city":"Chicago","pr":"Illinois","zip":"60611","s":"R","lat":41.85,"lon":-87.65,"c":"Esther Vorovich, MD"},{"f":"University of Chicago","city"